nds several days rather than trying to blast through it."," ",(0,t.jsx)(u,{href:"https://www.visitoregon.com/oregon-road-trips-guide/",children:"Visit Oregon +1"})]}),(0,t.jsx)("div",{className:"overflow-x-auto",role:"region","aria-label":"10-day route table",tabIndex:0,children:(0,t.jsxs)("table",{children:[(0,t.jsx)("thead",{children:(0,t.jsxs)("tr",{children:[(0,t.jsx)("th",{children:"Day"}),(0,t.jsx)("th",{children:"Sleep"}),(0,t.jsx)("th",{children:"The plan"})]})}),(0,t.jsx)("tbody",{children:n.w.map((e,a)=>(0,t.jsxs)("tr",{children:[(0,t.jsx)("td",{children:(0,t.jsx)("strong",{children:a+1})}),e.map((e,a)=>(0,t.jsx)("td",{children:e},a))]},a))})]})}),(0,t.jsx)("h3",{children:"Days 1–4 — Washington gets wild"}),(0,t.jsxs)("p",{children:["Start with ",(0,t.jsx)("strong",{children:"one night in Seattle"})," rather than treating it as merely an airport. Spend the afternoon around Pike Place Market and the waterfront, then have a serious dinner before the wilderness portion begins."]}),(0,t.jsxs)("p",{children:["Day 2, head for ",(0,t.jsx)("strong",{children:"Olympic National Park"}),". Hurricane Ridge gives you the alpine side of Olympic immediately; then sleep in"," ",(0,t.jsx)("strong",{children:"Port Angeles"}),"."]}),(0,t.jsxs)("p",{children:["Day 3 is one of my favorites:"," ",(0,t.jsx)("strong",{children:"Lake Crescent → Sol Duc Falls → Rialto Beach"}),". Sleep around Forks so you're positioned for the western side of the park."]}),(0,t.jsxs)("p",{children:["Day 4 is pure PNW fantasy:"," ",(0,t.jsx)("strong",{children:"Hoh Rainforest in the morning"}),", then"," ",(0,t.jsx)("strong",{children:"Ruby Beach around late afternoon/sunset"}),". Olympic really deserves several days because its alpine mountains, temperate rainforest and Pacific coastline are effectively three completely different destinations. A 3-day allocation is consistent with current 7–10 day park itineraries."," ",(0,t.jsx)(u,{href:"https://visitournationalparks.com/trip-idea/pacific-northwest-icons/",children:"Visit our National Parks"})]}),(0,t.jsxs)("p",{children:[(0,t.jsx)("strong",{children:"Don't rush Hoh."})," Do the easy Hall of Mosses, then walk farther along the Hoh River Trail until the crowds thin out."]}),(0,t.jsx)(d,{start:3}),(0,t.jsx)("h3",{children:"Days 5–7 — Highway 101"}),(0,t.jsxs)("p",{children:["Day 5, leave Olympic and follow the coast south. Stop for lunch in"," ",(0,t.jsx)("strong",{children:"Astoria"}),", cross into Oregon, and aim to reach"," ",(0,t.jsx)("strong",{children:"Cannon Beach by late afternoon"}),"."]}),(0,t.jsx)("p",{children:"Then walk the beach around Haystack Rock as the light starts dropping."}),(0,t.jsxs)("p",{children:[(0,t.jsx)("strong",{children:"Stay in Cannon Beach."})," This is one place where paying extra for an ocean-view room can actually be worth it."]}),(0,t.jsx)("p",{children:"Day 6 is the road-trip day I would most look forward to:"}),(0,t.jsx)("p",{children:(0,t.jsx)("strong",{children:"Cannon Beach → Manzanita → Tillamook → Cape Kiwanda/Pacific City → Depoe Bay → Yachats"})}),(0,t.jsxs)("p",{children:["Don't treat Highway 101 as transportation. Stop constantly. Oregon's beaches are public, so spontaneous beach stops are part of the experience."," ",(0,t.jsx)(u,{href:"https://www.visitoregon.com/oregon-coast/",children:"Visit Oregon +1"})]}),(0,t.jsxs)("p",{children:["Stay in ",(0,t.jsx)("strong",{children:"Yachats"}),", which is smaller and moodier than the better-known resort towns."]}),(0,t.jsxs)("p",{children:["Day 7, do ",(0,t.jsx)("strong",{children:"Cape Perpetua"})," early. Depending on tides, explore tide pools and the dramatic shoreline around Thor's Well, then stop in Newport for lunch before turning inland toward Portland. Tide timing materially changes the Oregon Coast experience, so check it each morning."," ",(0,t.jsx)(u,{href:"https://www.visitoregon.com/oregon-coast/",children:"Visit Oregon"})]}),(0,t.jsx)("h3",{children:"Days 8–10 — Portland, waterfalls & Mt. Hood"}),(0,t.jsxs)("p",{children:["Give ",(0,t.jsx)("strong",{children:"Portland"})," a full day. I'd keep this deliberately unstructured: coffee, neighborhoods, Powell's, food carts, maybe Forest Park, then a good dinner."]}),(0,t.jsxs)("p",{children:["On Day 9, head east into the ",(0,t.jsx)("strong",{children:"Columbia River Gorge"}),"."]}),(0,t.jsxs)("p",{children:["Do"," ",(0,t.jsx)("strong",{children:"Vista House → Latourell Falls → Multnomah Falls → Hood River"}),". If you want an actual hike rather than just viewpoints, substitute one waterfall stop for a longer trail."]}),(0,t.jsxs)("p",{children:["Stay overnight in ",(0,t.jsx)("strong",{children:"Hood River"}),". The Gorge contains more than 90 waterfalls, and Hood River is about an hour from Portland, so this section gives an enormous scenery payoff without a punishing drive."," ",(0,t.jsx)(u,{href:"https://www.visitoregon.com/columbia-river-gorge/",children:"Visit Oregon"})]}),(0,t.jsxs)("p",{children:["For your finale on Day 10, take OR-35 toward ",(0,t.jsx)("strong",{children:"Mt. Hood"}),", stop at ",(0,t.jsx)("strong",{children:"Timberline Lodge"}),", have lunch with the mountain looming over you, and loop back to Portland. Hood River to the Mt. Hood area is only about 45 minutes."," ",(0,t.jsx)(u,{href:"https://www.visitoregon.com/columbia-river-gorge/",children:"Visit Oregon"})]}),(0,t.jsx)(d,{start:6}),(0,t.jsx)("h3",{children:"A few choices that make this trip much better"}),(0,t.jsxs)("p",{children:["I'd do this ",(0,t.jsx)("strong",{children:"late June through September"})," for the greatest probability of mountain access; Washington's national-park road trips are especially reliable from roughly mid-July through September when seasonal roads are typically open."," ",(0,t.jsx)(u,{href:"https://www.earthtrekkers.com/washington-itinerary-national-parks-road-trip/",children:"Earth Trekkers"})," ","Early October can also be gorgeous, but mountain weather and seasonal closures become more consequential."]}),(0,t.jsxs)("p",{children:["Book"," ",(0,t.jsx)("strong",{children:"Olympic, Cannon Beach/Yachats, and Hood River first"}),". Those locations matter more than having the perfect hotel in Seattle or Portland."]}),(0,t.jsxs)("p",{children:["And don't add Bend, Crater Lake ",(0,t.jsx)("em",{children:"and"})," North Cascades just because they're nearby on a map. They aren't nearby in road-trip terms. Ten days is enough to experience the PNW rather than merely collect destinations."]}),(0,t.jsxs)("p",{children:[(0,t.jsx)("strong",{children:"My lodging split:"})," Seattle 1 → Port Angeles 1 → Forks 2 → Cannon Beach 1 → Yachats 1 → Portland 2 → Hood River 1 → departure. That gives you"," ",(0,t.jsx)("strong",{children:"3 national-park ecosystems + the Washington and Oregon coasts + Portland + the Gorge + Mt. Hood"})," ","in ten days, with only a couple of substantial driving days."]}),(0,t.jsx)("hr",{}),(0,t.jsx)("p",{children:"If you want, I can:"}),(0,t.jsxs)("ul",{children:[(0,t.jsx)("li",{children:"Add detailed daily morning activities to the itinerary"}),(0,t.jsx)("li",{children:"Include restaurant and food recommendations per stop"}),(0,t.jsx)("li",{children:"Suggest packing and preparation tips for each phase of the trip"})]})]})}function d({start:e}){return(0,t.jsx)("div",{className:"grid grid-cols-3 gap-1",children:n.e.slice(e,e+3).map(e=>(0,t.jsx)(a.default,{src:e.src,alt:e.alt,width:240,height:220,unoptimized:!0,className:"aspect-[1.2] size-full rounded-[12px] object-cover"},e.src))})}function u({href:e,children:a}){return(0,t.jsx)(o.default,{href:e,target:"_blank",rel:"noopener noreferrer",className:"rounded-full bg-(--iui-chip) px-2 py-0.5 text-[10px] text-(--iui-muted)",children:a})}var m=e.i(215453),p=e.i(784020),h=e.i(7284),f=e.i(467467),g=e.i(941395),x=e.i(741117),v=e.i(552297),y=e.i(49585),b=e.i(879002),w=e.i(976442),j=e.i(112439),M=e.i(127928);let k=(0,f.default)(()=>e.A(409322),{loadableGenerated:{modules:[292978]},ssr:!1,loading:j.f});function N(){let{colorSchem